# Opt115 + Opt116 + Opt117 (2026-10-31, config LR; each inert unless set). Prompt-path scratch the grouped EXL3 MoE arm never reads is no longer borrowed
# from the card's expert slots, so the long-prompt loan falls 1201 -> 1060 slots at 33K (config LP -> LR), every one a resident expert back on the 3090.
# Opt116 STRATA_PF_EXL3_SLIM=1: on an EXL3 pack with the grouped prompt kernel, exl3_moe runs every expert Xs -> Dm with its own gate/up and down scratch,
#   so the FP16 dequant path's GU (T x K x 1280 fp32) and Hh (T x K x 640 fp16) are neither allocated nor counted (~190 MiB at a 3072-token chunk).
# Opt117 STRATA_PF_EXL3_NOXS=1: the expert library's new exl3s_prefill_moe_tok (exl3/strata_m4/exl3_strata_pf_host.cu, config LR) reads each sorted row's
#   input at its token in the [T][N] fp16 activations, so the gathered [T x K][N] copy Xs (150 MiB at 3072 tokens) goes too. Resolved at run time from the
#   loaded library (dladdr / dlopen RTLD_NOLOAD / dlsym); without it the request stops with an error instead of falling back.
# Opt115 STRATA_PF_LOAN_DUMP=1: diagnostic, one stderr line per loan section (gemm, chunk bufs, group, set scratch, dq + mmq, ring, mac x/y, kv stage).
# Numerics: the same kernels read the same row values: bit-identical to config LP.
# Measured (ABBA vs config LP, fresh restart per arm): 33K 1003.0 -> 1013.6 tok/s (+1.06 %), 8K 852.0 -> 866.8 (+1.7 %), 2.5K 288.3 -> 289.4.
